1
00:00:02,543 --> 00:00:07,150
Two hundred "tests", each one is green;

2
00:00:07,811 --> 00:00:13,218
The finest score you've ever seen!

3
00:00:12,928 --> 00:00:15,667
My "tests"? I paste app code in haste:

4
00:00:15,377 --> 00:00:17,460
A perfect duplication!

5
00:00:17,403 --> 00:00:19,905
The sums agree! How sweet for me!

6
00:00:19,615 --> 00:00:22,163
A shared miscalculation.

7
00:00:21,873 --> 00:00:24,601
With screenshots, commas cause such dramas:

8
00:00:24,311 --> 00:00:26,604
A red notification.

9
00:00:26,314 --> 00:00:29,006
My "test"? Fantastic, automatic—

10
00:00:28,716 --> 00:00:31,167
I change its expectation!

11
00:00:30,877 --> 00:00:33,361
To boost my score, I cover more;

12
00:00:33,071 --> 00:00:35,130
They've trained me just to make the grade.

13
00:00:35,248 --> 00:00:38,046
Like kids in class, I aim to pass;

14
00:00:37,756 --> 00:00:40,325
The marks decide how tests get made.

15
00:00:41,523 --> 00:00:43,195
Did you actually test it?

16
00:00:42,905 --> 00:00:45,434
Press it, stress it, second-guess it?

17
00:00:45,865 --> 00:00:47,682
Find a clue? Congratulations!

18
00:00:47,392 --> 00:00:50,043
Now pursue its implications.

19
00:00:50,445 --> 00:00:55,217
What did you try? What did you find?

20
00:00:51,548 --> 00:00:53,114
(What did you try?)

21
00:00:53,754 --> 00:00:55,436
(What did you find?)

22
00:00:54,927 --> 00:00:59,029
What changed your mind?

23
00:00:59,971 --> 00:01:02,630
The gym? No net. We log a set;

24
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:04,714
The app says "Saved!"—but what's in store?

25
00:01:04,424 --> 00:01:06,941
Reload the screen; no set is seen.

26
00:01:06,839 --> 00:01:09,201
Connect once more: still gone? Explore!

27
00:01:08,911 --> 00:01:11,359
We chase the clue; try something new:

28
00:01:11,314 --> 00:01:13,735
Connect, then save; the sets all stay.

29
00:01:13,445 --> 00:01:16,109
We drop the net, then save a set;

30
00:01:15,819 --> 00:01:18,476
A new check flags what went away.

31
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:20,120
Did you actually test it?

32
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:22,383
Press it, stress it, second-guess it?

33
00:01:22,802 --> 00:01:24,613
Find a clue? Congratulations!

34
00:01:24,323 --> 00:01:26,945
Now pursue its implications.

35
00:01:27,435 --> 00:01:31,676
What did you try? What did you find?

36
00:01:28,532 --> 00:01:30,196
(What did you try?)

37
00:01:30,807 --> 00:01:32,454
(What did you find?)

38
00:01:31,905 --> 00:01:36,094
What changed your mind?

39
00:01:36,920 --> 00:01:39,493
A fresh bot crew? Here's what to do:

40
00:01:39,203 --> 00:01:41,953
Real browsers, a playbook, and users in mind.

41
00:01:41,663 --> 00:01:44,060
The goals you name will guide the game;

42
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:46,394
Your oracles help them to judge what they find.

43
00:01:46,104 --> 00:01:48,454
One probes the chat—just me and Pat:

44
00:01:48,164 --> 00:01:50,933
Does Sam's new account show the text Pat just sent?

45
00:01:50,643 --> 00:01:53,104
One tests the cart, then hits restart:

46
00:01:52,814 --> 00:01:55,467
Do orders still match what the customer spent?

47
00:01:55,177 --> 00:01:57,708
We trade the news, compare the views;

48
00:01:57,418 --> 00:01:59,931
We share the doubts and observations.

49
00:01:59,641 --> 00:02:02,855
Some calls need you. We'll talk them through;

50
00:02:02,990 --> 00:02:08,196
We ask for fresh interpretations.

51
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:11,645
A check applies a rule we've set;

52
00:02:11,355 --> 00:02:13,874
It tells us if that rule is met.

53
00:02:13,584 --> 00:02:16,109
To test, we ask what else—and why;

54
00:02:15,819 --> 00:02:18,430
Each clue can change what next we try.

55
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,597
A check reports, "The sums agree!"

56
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:22,895
We test: "Could both be wrong? Let's see!"

57
00:02:22,605 --> 00:02:25,165
The checks are part of how we test;

58
00:02:24,875 --> 00:02:27,642
We judge what serves the users best.

59
00:02:28,799 --> 00:02:30,371
Did you actually test it?

60
